Q: log4j does not load Kotlin @Plugin class A: <p>Log4j creates a <code>Log4j2Plugins.dat</code> file to cache all of the <code>@Plugin</code> annotated classes it finds in a project. This is generated as output via Log4j's <code>PluginProcessor</code> (<a href="https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/blob/f10c986684283e44e01149bbcc5f759f06e33c9a/log4j-core/src/main/java/org/apache/logging/log4j/core/config/plugins/processor/PluginProcessor.java" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Source</a>), which can be configured in Maven or Gradle by following <a href="https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/plugins.html#plugin-registry" rel="nofollow noreferrer">these instructions</a>.</p>
<p>Unfortunately, Log4j's <code>PluginProcessor</code> is for processing <em>Java</em> annotations. For <em>Kotlin</em> annotations, we need to use <code>kapt</code> (<a href="https://kotlinlang.org/docs/kapt.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Docs</a>). That can be configured to run Java annotation processor at the appropriate time in the Kotlin compilation lifecycle.</p>
<p>For example, I have a custom Log4j2 Appender in my <code>src/test/kotlin</code> directory. I then configured <code>kapt</code> to run during the <code>generate-test-resources</code> phase like so:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>    &lt;build&gt;
        &lt;plugins&gt;
            &lt;!-- This generates the metadata for Log4j2 to discover classes annotated with a @Plugin Annotation --&gt;
            &lt;plugin&gt;
                &lt;groupId&gt;org.jetbrains.kotlin&lt;/groupId&gt;
                &lt;artifactId&gt;kotlin-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
                &lt;artifactId&gt;${kotlin.version}&lt;/artifactId&gt;
                &lt;executions&gt;
                    &lt;execution&gt;
                        &lt;id&gt;test-kapt&lt;/id&gt;
                        &lt;phase&gt;generate-test-resources&lt;/phase&gt;
                        &lt;goals&gt;
                            &lt;goal&gt;test-kapt&lt;/goal&gt;
                        &lt;/goals&gt;
                        &lt;configuration&gt;
                            &lt;annotationProcessorPaths&gt;
                                &lt;annotationProcessorPath&gt;
                                    &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.logging.log4j&lt;/groupId&gt;
                                    &lt;artifactId&gt;log4j-core&lt;/artifactId&gt;
                                    &lt;version&gt;${log4j2.version}&lt;/version&gt;
                                &lt;/annotationProcessorPath&gt;
                            &lt;/annotationProcessorPaths&gt;
                        &lt;/configuration&gt;
                    &lt;/execution&gt;
                &lt;/executions&gt;
            &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;/plugins&gt;
    &lt;/build&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Now when I run the following, the <code>Log4j2Plugins.dat</code> file will be generated as expected:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>mvn generate-test-resources
</code></pre>
<p>If your <code>@Plugin</code>-annotated classes are in <code>src/main/kotlin</code>, you'll need to use the <code>generate-resources</code> goal instead of <code>generate-test-resources</code>.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>NOTE:</strong> Unfortunately, <code>kapt</code> will not run when the project is built within IntelliJ (<a href="https://kotlinlang.org/docs/kapt.html#use-in-intellij-build-system" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Source</a>):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>kapt is not supported for IntelliJ IDEA's own build system. Launch the build from the &quot;Maven Projects&quot; toolbar whenever you want to re-run the annotation processing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you're using IntelliJ, you can get around this by adding a &quot;Before Launch Task&quot; to run the <code>generate-test-resources</code> (or <code>generate-resources</code>) as part of your run configurations. Here's how mine is configured to run the goal on a child <code>test</code> module:</p>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/DdiCUan4.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/DdiCUan4.png" alt="Screenshot of &quot;Before Launch&quot; tasks configured in IntelliJ" /></a></p>
<p>This will add a few seconds to the run configuration's runtime, but it's a way to ensure other engineers using IntelliJ will have the generated <code>Log4j2Plugins.dat</code> file.</p>
